Below is some information about how selective admission for the winter semester 2026/2027 was. It all depends a lot on whether you have citizenship, a Bachelor's degree or a previous Master's degree from inside the European Economic Area (the EEA, that is the EU plus Iceland, Liechtenstein and Norway) or whether you are from outside the EEA. Legally, we can only admit few applicants from outside the EEA when we have barely enough places for applicants from within the EEA. As a result, admission for non-EEA applicants has become much more selective than it used to be until just one year before. To find out more, please click on the programs below.

